+# Audit: wide screens (0.21.0)
+
+Date: 2026-11-03 · PR: Cochilo 0.25.0 · Auditor: Claude (graphic-design-fundamentals + impeccable)
+
+## Scope
+
+Cochilo `size` gains `rail` (80), `content-max` (600), `width-medium` (600) and `width-expanded`
+(840), Android's window classes. components.md: the Navigation rail row, and Cochilo's two panes
+when expanded. No colour changes; contrast unchanged.
+
+## graphic-design-fundamentals (§13 checklist)
+
+| # | Question | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Brief | Pass: a tablet or unfolded phone shows more without stretching lines |
+| 2 | Concept | Pass: the same tabs on their side; Today never leaves the screen when there's room |
+| 3 | Hierarchy | Pass: Today's one teal action still leads; the second pane is secondary |
+| 4 | Contrast | Pass: unchanged |
+| 5 | Alignment and grid | Pass: the column centres at 600dp; panes split evenly with a hairline |
+| 6 | Spacing | Pass: the rail's items sit space3 apart, from space4 at the top |
+| 7 | Typography | Pass: unchanged roles; line length stays under ~80 characters |
+| 8 | Colour | Pass: the rail uses `surface` and the `selected` pill, like the tab bar |
+| 9 | Consistency | Pass: one component, three widths |
+| 10 | Simplicity | Pass: no new chrome on phones |
+| 11 | Real-size test | Pass: Cochilo's tablet (800dp) and foldable (841dp) screenshots |
+| 12 | Accessibility and ergonomics | Pass: 48dp targets, Role.Tab, a selectable group |
+| 13 | Production | Pass: tokens generated, drift 0 |
+
+## impeccable (audit, native / Android)
+
+| # | Dimension | Score | Key finding |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Accessibility | 4 | Same semantics as the tab bar |
+| 2 | Performance | 4 | Two panes compose two screens; no extra work on phones |
+| 3 | Appearance & theming | 4 | All three themes from the same roles |
+| 4 | Platform conformance | 4 | Material window classes and NavigationRail placement |
+| 5 | Adaptivity | 4 | Compact, medium and expanded each have a layout |
+| | **Total** | **20/20** | |
